<BaseLayout title="Early access terms — deployment draft" description="Early access terms — deployment draft" lang="en">
<main class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16"><a href="/" class="text-indigo-600">Signalist</a><h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mt-8 mb-10">Early access terms — deployment draft</h1>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Service scope</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Signalist organizes RSS content, supports team curation, prepares newsletter and social drafts, and provides optional integrations. Features requiring provider accounts remain unavailable until configured. This repository does not define a commercial service-level agreement.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Responsible use</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Use sources and content you are entitled to access and share. Review generated summaries and every public post for accuracy and publishing rights. Do not place secrets or sensitive personal data in articles, notes or post drafts.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Publishing and external services</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Public publishing requires your explicit approval. Remote platforms control their API access, fees and availability. A lost response can leave a publication or synchronization outcome uncertain; check the remote account before creating another job. Disconnecting erases local authorization; revoke app access in provider settings as well.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Plans and cancellation</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Paid plans are charged per seat only through a configured checkout. Final prices and billing terms must be shown by the operator before purchase. This build provides no automatic early-access discount. Cancel an active subscription before deleting the billed account or its sole-member workspace.</p></section>
<section class="mb-8"><h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Operator terms pending</h2><p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Before public launch, the operator must supply legal identity, support contact, applicable law, payment and refund terms, acceptable-use enforcement and service commitments. This document is a software deployment draft, not an executed agreement.</p></section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
